We’ll use a local MCP server over stdio. The Deep Agent program starts/connects to that server automatically.
The current LangChain first-party MCP integration uses `MCPAdapter`,
which turns MCP tools into normal LangChain tools.


FastMCP automatically creates the MCP tool schema from the Python function, type hints, and docstring.
Its default run() transport is stdio, which is ideal for a local MCP server


We do not need to separately start course_mcp_server.py.
The MCP client configuration launches the local server process over stdio.
FastMCP supports exactly this local server pattern.


We should get output roughly like:

========== MCP TOOLS DISCOVERED ==========

Tool Name: get_course_details
Description: Get the duration and fee of a training course.
--------------------------------------------------


========== FINAL ANSWER ==========

The Agentic AI course lasts 6 weeks and costs €600.


